      "id": 1,
      "text": "Hunter was founded in 1887 when John Hunter, a stockholder of the Missouri Lumber and Mining Company, built a sawmill on the site.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        17
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hunter%2C_Missouri"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The town’s first railroad depot, erected in 1889, was the second building constructed after the sawmill.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hunter%2C_Missouri"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Hunter grew into a logging boomtown, with the company store, hotel, and a logging camp all opening across the street from the depot.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        7
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hunter%2C_Missouri"
    },
    {
